properties.statement:
Reading a requirement answers "which reports, at what confidence, does this requirement rest on" in one read: the walk follows GOVERNED_BY into the governing decision's chain. reason_to_exist names more than the top of the chain. When a claim is replaced (`replaces`), the steps that used it are flagged or rewired, so a superseded assessment part does not silently keep a decision's chain holding.
MEASURED 2026-10-19 in the capstone:
- reasoning_report on each requirement walked 1 claim, rests_on [], "unsupported";
- reason_to_exist named only the decision and its first step;
- after A2 was replaced by A2b, A2 still fed dec:handle-pulse-to-pulse-agility ("stays_on_replaced").
